This is a forwarded bug report I sent a week ago. Along with a bug summary
and system info, there's also a github link for test scripts and output
pcap files from both the improper ath9k_htc transmissions, and the expected
transmissions from a different softmac wifi card. Let me know if any other
info should be included - this is my first bug report.

---------- Forwarded message ---------
From: Manasseh Pawlos <manassehpawlos@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, Sep 18, 2026 at 6:40=E2=80=AFPM
Subject: AR9271 ignores Radiotap TX_FLAGS field for injected frames
To: <toke@toke.dk>


Hello!

When injecting 802.11b frames on a fresh installation of Fedora 44 (kernel
7.2, untainted), frames transmitted through my AR9271 USB Wi-fi adapter in
monitor mode have their sequence number overwritten, and will re-transmit
to get an ACK regardless of if I disable these behaviors using the TX_FLAGS
field in the Radiotap header. These flags are obeyed on my other SoftMAC
USB adapter (AWUS036ACM using the r8169 driver), so presumably this is an
ath9k_htc - specific bug.

Dmesg and Kernel-Config dump are included below, as well as a link to the
Python scripts I used, and the resulting Wireshark captures, both from the
AR9271 itself, and from the r8169 adapter.

Please let me know if there's any way I can help with this! I'm willing to
rebuild my kernel, apply patches, or supply more info as needed.

Github link with more info:
https://github.com/manassehpawlos-oss/Radiotap-Frame-Injection-Troubleshoot=
ing.git

